# The one GPUI bridge (ADR 0003, decision 2): `background(cx, key, priority, f) -> BackgroundTask<T>`
# in lector-ui is the only file where UI code may name or hold a GPUI executor
# (`BackgroundExecutor`, `ForegroundExecutor`) or call `background_executor()`.
# Why it needs it: the bridge takes the executors of the caller's GPUI context through
# `BridgeContext` to deliver results on the foreground executor and to detect GPUI's test
# dispatcher (`bg.dispatcher.as_test()`), so tests stay deterministic. It spawns nothing on them:
# jobs run on the lector-app scheduler.
# (Before ADR 0010 item 8 the rule only matched two method names, which this file did not use, so
# it needed no entry; naming an executor type is now found, so it does.)
crates/lector-ui/src/background.rs
